# Template files contain shell heredocs ($(cat <<BODY...BODY)) at column 0 inside
# YAML run: blocks, which breaks prettier's YAML parser. Templates must not be formatted.
scripts/templates/*.yml
scripts/propagation/templates/*.yml

# Append-only agent-ping ledgers — operational logs, NOT prose. proseWrap:always would
# reflow the whole 150KB+ file on every single ping append (huge churn) and races the
# orphan-ping cron's writes. Left literal so appends stay a clean diff.
*_orchestrator/_agent_pings.md
plans/active/_agent_pings.md

# Auto-generated CI/CD workflow catalog — owned by scripts/generate-workflow-catalog.py (deterministic
# emitter). prettier would re-pad the tables → false drift vs the generator output on every regen.
docs/repo-management/CICD-WORKFLOW-CATALOG.md

# Byte-exact snapshots of the GitHub-HOSTED form of every workflow (scripts/self-hosted-runners/
# hosted-baseline.sh). Reformatting them defeats the entire purpose: the value is the EXACT bytes
# that ran on GitHub-hosted, so a revert is a copy rather than an archaeology exercise. Prettier DID
# rewrite them once (2026-07-16, long `description:` rewrapped) — the live workflows are only
# formatted when staged, so the copies drifted from their own source the moment they were committed.
scripts/self-hosted-runners/hosted-baseline/*.yml

# Canonical form is OWNED by scripts/quality_gates/check_workspace_manifest_canonical.py
# (json.dumps(obj, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n" — always fully expanded arrays, no
# per-line "fill"), matching the ~17 internal Python writers (update-repo-version /
# staging-to-main / sit-unlock / merge-driver / consolidator / monitors). Prettier's own
# array-fill heuristic (collapse onto one line when it fits printWidth) produces a DIFFERENT,
# incompatible byte form for short arrays and is idempotent on it — once prettier touches this
# file the two writers fight forever. Confirmed 2026-07-17: a tree-wide `prettier --write` swept
# this file in via the generic **/*.json glob and broke manifest-canonical QG.
workspace-manifest.json
